  "method": "Fresh 20-turn API runs. Baseline updates five scores each turn. Selective updates uncertain fields and accepts explicit categorical changes to settled fields; each field is settled when its most likely value reaches the threshold. Both include the first snapshot-creation call. Model reported tokens only; no tool calls or local storage costs measured.",
  "instructions": {
    "baseline": "Maintain current beliefs for a travel-support conversation. Each input JSON has new_message and previous_beliefs containing the saved belief values. Return probabilities for the current primary request: book_flight, book_hotel, or unknown if it is neither. These three probabilities should sum to 1. Return independent probabilities for budget_sensitive (prefers a low price) and prefers_direct (prefers a nonstop flight). The latest explicit change overrides older statements; otherwise preferences persist. Base the result only on the supplied context.",
    "selective": "Maintain decision state for a travel-support conversation. The input contains the new_message and previous_state. Previous_state separates settled categorical values from uncertain probability values. Return new probabilities only for fields listed in update_confidence_for. For the other, settled fields, put an item in changes only when the new message explicitly changes their saved value; do not repeat unchanged values. The current primary intent is book_flight, book_hotel, or unknown if neither. budget_sensitive means a preference for a low price. prefers_direct means a preference for a nonstop flight. The latest explicit change overrides older statements; otherwise values persist. Intent probabilities should sum to 1. Base the result only on supplied input."
